## CQRS with Dispatcher (Mandatory)

Controllers MUST use `Dispatcher` â€” never depend on handlers directly.

```
Controller â†’ Dispatcher â†’ QueryHandler/CommandHandler â†’ Result
```

### Controller Pattern

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/bff/containers")
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class ContainerSearchController {
    
    // ONLY dependency is Dispatcher
    private final Dispatcher dispatcher;
    
    @GetMapping("/search/{backend}")
    public ResponseEntity<ContainerSearchResponse> search(
            @PathVariable ExternalApiProvider backend,
            @RequestParam("q") @ValidContainerNumber String containerNumber) {
        
        // Sanitize input
        var sanitized = InputSanitizer.sanitizeContainerNumber(containerNumber);
        
        // Create query
        var query = SearchContainersQuery.fromCode(backend, sanitized, "I");
        
        // Dispatch and handle result
        var results = dispatcher.dispatch(query)
            .getOrThrow(error -> new DomainErrorException(error, mapErrorToHttpStatus(error)));
        
        return ResponseEntity.ok(ContainerSearchResponse.fromApplication(results));
    }
}
```

## Vertical Slice Architecture

Features are organized by business capability:

```
application/features/
â”œâ”€â”€ auth/
â”‚   â”œâ”€â”€ authorization/     # GetAuthorizationUrlQuery + Handler + Result
â”‚   â”œâ”€â”€ token/             # ExchangeAuthCodeCommand, RefreshTokenCommand
â”‚   â”œâ”€â”€ logout/            # BuildLogoutUrlCommand + Handler + Result
â”‚   â”œâ”€â”€ userinfo/          # GetUserInfoQuery + Handler + Result
â”‚   â”œâ”€â”€ account/           # GetAccountUrlsQuery + Handler + Result
â”‚   â””â”€â”€ common/            # KeycloakAuthPort (shared interface)
â””â”€â”€ containersearch/
    â”œâ”€â”€ single/            # SearchContainersQuery + Handler
    â”œâ”€â”€ bulk/              # BulkSearchContainersQuery + Handler + Results
    â””â”€â”€ common/            # ContainerSearchStrategy (interface), shared DTOs
```

**Feature Rules:**
- Features MUST NOT depend on each other (isolated slices)
- Classes MUST be in flow-based sub-packages (e.g., `auth.token`, not `auth`)
- Port interfaces MUST be in `common/` sub-packages
- Strategy interfaces are defined in application layer, implemented in infrastructure

## Token Pass-Through Strategy

### JWT Propagation via Interceptor

```java
@Component
public class TokenPropagationInterceptor implements ClientHttpRequestInterceptor {
    
    @Override
    public ClientHttpResponse intercept(
            HttpRequest request, 
            byte[] body, 
            ClientHttpRequestExecution execution) throws IOException {
        
        var authentication = SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication();
        
        if (authentication instanceof JwtAuthenticationToken jwtAuth) {
            var token = jwtAuth.getToken().getTokenValue();
            request.getHeaders().setBearerAuth(token);
        }
        
        return execution.execute(request, body);
    }
}
```

## Parallel Aggregation Pattern

Use `CompletableFuture` for independent calls with virtual threads:

```java
@Service
public class BulkSearchContainersQueryHandler 
        implements QueryHandler<BulkSearchContainersQuery, Result<BulkContainerSearchResult>> {
    
    @Override
    public Result<BulkContainerSearchResult> handle(BulkSearchContainersQuery query) {
        // Execute searches in parallel using virtual threads
        var futures = query.containerIds().stream()
            .map(containerId -> CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(
                () -> searchSingle(containerId, query)
            ))
            .toList();
        
        // Wait for all to complete
        CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0])).join();
        
        // Collect results and failures
        var results = futures.stream()
            .map(CompletableFuture::join)
            .toList();
        
        return Result.success(aggregateResults(results));
    }
}
```

## Naming Conventions (Enforced by ArchUnit)

| Type | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Controllers | `*Controller` with `@RestController` | `ContainerSearchController` |
| Query Handlers | `*QueryHandler` with `@Service` | `SearchContainersQueryHandler` |
| Command Handlers | `*CommandHandler` with `@Service` | `ExchangeAuthCodeCommandHandler` |
| Queries | `*Query` record implementing `Query<T>` | `SearchContainersQuery` |
| Commands | `*Command` record implementing `Command<T>` | `RefreshTokenCommand` |
| Results | `*Result` record | `ContainerSearchResult` |
| Ports | `*Port` interface in `common/` | `KeycloakAuthPort` |
| Strategies | `*Strategy` interface | `ContainerSearchStrategy` |
| Web DTOs | `*Request`, `*Response` records | `BulkContainerSearchRequest` |
| Infrastructure DTOs | `*Dto` records | `EModalContainerDto` |
| HTTP Clients | `*Client` interface | `EModalClient` |
| Adapters | `*Adapter` class | `KeycloakAuthAdapter` |
| Filters | `*Filter` extending `OncePerRequestFilter` | `CorrelationIdFilter` |
| Interceptors | `*Interceptor` implementing `ClientHttpRequestInterceptor` | `TokenPropagationInterceptor` |

## BFF Layer Responsibilities

| Responsibility | BFF Layer | Backend APIs |
|----------------|-----------|--------------|
| Authentication | Token validation & pass-through | Service-specific authorization |
| Aggregation | Combine multiple API responses | Return domain-specific data |
| Transformation | Convert to client-friendly DTOs | Return service DTOs |
| Error Handling | User-friendly ProblemDetail | Domain errors |
| Rate Limiting | Client rate limiting | Service protection |
| Resilience | Circuit breakers, retries | None |

## Conventions

- BFF endpoints should be client-specific, not generic pass-throughs
- Use meaningful BFF paths (e.g., `/api/bff/containers`, not `/api/containers`)
- Always transform backend DTOs to client-friendly responses
- Implement circuit breakers for all backend calls
- Support partial failures gracefully (return what you can)
- Use parallel aggregation when calls are independent
- Pass authentication tokens to backends via interceptors
- Keep BFF logic thin â€” it's a facade, not a domain layer
- **Controllers MUST only depend on `Dispatcher`** â€” enforced by ArchUnit

**See also:** `cqrs.mdc`, `http-clients.mdc`, `aggregation.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`
